the driver would have been paid 80 percent of it, SGD 3.60, under POL-NS-07 — the anti-farming test does not trip, because driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 against 110 completed trips in 30 days (the tests are 4 or more, and a rate above 0.08).\n\nThe rider's statement that this is 'the third time' is not borne out: the record shows 2 disputes between this pair, not 3. But 2 is already at the escalation threshold, so that point does not change the outcome.\n\nThe open question for the reviewer: whether the repeated no-show disputes between this rider and this driver show a rider who repeatedly fails to appear (in which case the SGD 4.50 fee stands and SGD 3.60 is paid to the driver under POL-NS-07), or repeated mis-cancellation by the driver (in which case the fee is refunded to the rider), or a mix of both.\n\nA note on the profile material: lifetime counters such as prior_no_show_flags were treated as context only and were not used as a ground, as POL-GEN-01 requires."
